\description{
\code{binomial_test()} tests whether the observed proportion of a binary
variable differs from a hypothesized proportion. It uses the exact binomial
test, making it valid for any sample size.

Think of it as:
\itemize{
\item Testing whether a coin is fair (proportion of heads = 50 percent)
\item Checking if your sample's gender ratio matches the population
\item Verifying if satisfaction rates meet a target proportion
}

The test tells you:
\itemize{
\item Whether the observed proportion differs significantly from the expected
\item The exact p-value (based on the binomial distribution)
\item A confidence interval for the true proportion
}
